│   Message:                                                                                       │
│     I fixed the traceback recursion in `rich/traceback.py` by making the exception-chain walk    │
│ skip any exception it has already visited, so a cause or context cycle can no longer loop        │
│ forever. The patch is submitted (one file, 10 insertions, 2 deletions).                          │
│                                                                                                  │
│     The change adds a `seen_exceptions` set in `Traceback.extract`, records each exception's id  │
│ as it is processed, and skips a `__cause__` or `__context__` whose id is already in the set. I   │
│ also added `Set` to the `typing` imports.                                                        │
│                                                                                                  │
│     I checked it with a self-referencing `__context__` case, which now yields 2 stacks instead   │
│ of hanging, and `tests/test_traceback.py` passes (21 passed, 1 skipped). I did not add a test    │
│ for the cycle case, and the issue text was only a title, so the fix is based on my reading of    │
│ the two linked issues rather than their stated reproducers.                                      │
